From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iwinfo: report backend scan failures to callers

An unsuccessful backend scan is not a successful empty scan. Propagate the
native failure while retaining an empty results array for a successful scan
that found no BSS entries. Release the native owner on both outcomes.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

--- a/iwinfo.c
+++ b/iwinfo.c
@@ -378,7 +378,7 @@
                 struct ubus_request_data *req, const char *method,
                 struct blob_attr *msg)
 {
-	int i, rv, len, band;
+	int i, rv, len = 0, band;
 	void *c, *d, *t;
 	char mac[18];
 	char res[IWINFO_BUFSIZE];
@@ -389,11 +389,17 @@
 	if (rv)
 		return rv;
 
+	rv = iw->scanlist(ifname, res, &len);
+	if (rv) {
+		rpc_iwinfo_close();
+		return UBUS_STATUS_UNKNOWN_ERROR;
+	}
+
 	blob_buf_init(&buf, 0);
 
 	c = blobmsg_open_array(&buf, "results");
 
-	if (!iw->scanlist(ifname, res, &len) && (len > 0))
+	if (len > 0)
 	{
 		for (i = 0; i < len; i += sizeof(struct iwinfo_scanlist_entry))
 		{
